From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: gennro <gennro2004@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 29 Sep 2026 18:48:58 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 50/57] pan/bi: don't hoist shared values out of unified IDVS
 blocks (06n-arch)

On v12+ the vertex shader is one binary with a predicated block per
output stage, and nir_opt_gcm hoisted everything the blocks share in
front of them. Each hoisted value then stays live across all the
blocks: DXVK vertex shaders no longer fit in 64 registers, and in Deep
Rock Galactic 185 of 390 spilled (112k fills in all), leaving the frame
bound by vertex load/store. Without the hoist 85 spill (19k fills) and
the game goes from 30 to 35 fps. PAN_IDVS_HOIST=1 restores the hoist.
---
 src/panfrost/compiler/bifrost/bifrost_nir.c | 13 +++++++++++--
 1 file changed, 11 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/panfrost/compiler/bifrost/bifrost_nir.c b/src/panfrost/compiler/bifrost/bifrost_nir.c
index 99db2dbbff3..834c6403f4d 100644
--- a/src/panfrost/compiler/bifrost/bifrost_nir.c
+++ b/src/panfrost/compiler/bifrost/bifrost_nir.c
@@ -11,6 +11,7 @@
 #include "panfrost/compiler/pan_nir.h"
 #include "panfrost/compiler/pan_nir_prolog.h"
 #include "util/perf/cpu_trace.h"
+#include "util/u_debug.h"
 
 #include "panfrost/model/pan_model.h"
 #include "valhall/valhall.h"
@@ -1330,8 +1331,16 @@ bifrost_handle_unified_idvs_shader(nir_shader *nir)
       NIR_PASS(progress, nir, nir_opt_cse);
    }
 
-   /* Hoist common values before the predicated blocks. */
-   NIR_PASS(_, nir, nir_opt_gcm, true);
+   /* 06n-arch: don't hoist the values the predicated blocks share. Hoisted,
+    * each one stays live across all the blocks, and DXVK vertex shaders
+    * then no longer fit in 64 registers: in Deep Rock Galactic 185 of 390
+    * spilled, 112k fills in all, and the frame was bound by vertex
+    * load/store. Without the hoist the shared work is done once per block
+    * instead, which is cheap next to the fills: 85 spill, 19k fills, and
+    * 30 -> 35 fps. PAN_IDVS_HOIST=1 restores the hoist.
+    */
+   if (debug_get_bool_option("PAN_IDVS_HOIST", false))
+      NIR_PASS(_, nir, nir_opt_gcm, true);
 }
 
 static const char *
